Spec: Plugin Add Command

Purpose:
  Install a named SpecDD plugin from a Git repository into the current project.

Owns:
  ./add.ts
  ./add.test.ts

References:
  /src/services/plugin-installer/plugin-installer.sdd

Must:
  Receive a @PluginAddCommandContainer dependency object.
  Return an `add` command for attachment beneath the `plugin` group.
  Expose the command syntax `specdd plugin add <repository> <pluginname> [version]`.
  Describe the optional version in help as a branch, tag, or commit reachable from a branch or tag.
  Pass the repository, plugin name, optional version, and absolute current working directory to @PluginInstaller.add.
  Preserve an omitted version as absent so source resolution can distinguish omission from an explicit Git ref named `latest`.
  Reject missing required arguments and extra positional arguments before invoking the service.

Must not:
  Resolve Git refs, download plugin files, or write the plugin registry directly.

Depends on:
  @PluginInstaller
  Node.js current working directory

Exposes:
  @createPluginAddCommand
  @PluginAddCommandContainer

Scenario: explicit version
  Given the current directory is `/project`
  When `specdd plugin add \@acme/specdd-plugins review v1.2.0` runs
  Then @PluginInstaller.add receives `/project`, `\@acme/specdd-plugins`, `review`, and `v1.2.0`

Scenario: omitted version
  When `specdd plugin add \@acme/specdd-plugins review` runs
  Then @PluginInstaller.add receives no requested version
